t may turn either off but never on, exactly as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dynamic_registration"},{"text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this tenant’s"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"domains or ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this tenant’s"}]},{"text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OidcPolicy"},{"text":"] already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"text":". # Every bound here is a security control","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::min_cache_secs"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_cache_secs"},{"text":"] are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row written by hand cannot lift them.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],